# RTL↔software co-sim via DPI (M26 research)

**Last updated:** 2026-08-22  
**Refs:** Verilator 5.050 connecting guide (DPI-C); Helios RTL (yale-paragon) uses **file/Vivado** TBs, not DPI; IEEE 1800 DPI-C; Aether M16–M24 file goldens.

## Goal

Drive grow/peel RTL from **live Rust goldens** (`decode_cosim` / `helios_pe`) instead of only `rtl/gen/*.sv` includes — Progress “DPI Rust↔RTL co-sim”.

## Alternatives

| Option | Pros | Cons | Verdict |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Keep file `include` goldens (M20–M24) | Works Icarus+Verilator; proven | Stale if software drifts without regen | Keep as regression |
| **DPI-C import from SV → Rust `cdylib`** | IEEE; Verilator-supported; goldens computed in Rust at sim start | Icarus DPI weak; large Stim graphs need flat buffers | **Adopt for Blueprint (M26)** |
| Marlin / svdpi-rs frameworks | Rust ergonomics | Extra young deps; not needed for scalar Blueprint API | Reject for now |
| cocotb / Python driver | Fast to write | Not Rust↔RTL; duplicates Stim harness | Reject for this Next |
| Verilator C++ main + FFI (no SV `import`) | Full control | Not DPI as named in Progress | Defer |
| More OSD shots at p≈0.005 | Could tighten Wilson | Separate Next; M25 already denser curve | Not this milestone |

## Adopted M26 shape

1. Crate `aether_uf_dpi` (`cdylib`): `aether_dpi_load(case)` fills buffers from shared Blueprint graphs + `helios_pe` / `decode_cosim`.
2. `rtl/tb_aether_uf_dpi.sv` imports DPI getters; runs same DUT as decode TB.
3. Verilator `--binary` links `libaether_uf_dpi` (macOS `.dylib` / Linux `.so`).
4. File-based Icarus Blueprint TB remains the non-DPI regression.

